\cf3 \cb4 # PROJECT GUIDE \'96 AI-POWERED AUTOMATION WRITER (Home Assistant + n8n + GPT)\cf5  This project enables Home Assistant to generate, write, and activate automations using natural language. ChatGPT interprets user intent \uc0\u8594  n8n packages YAML \u8594  Home Assistant writes it into `/config/packages/` and reloads automations. This document explains: \cf6 -\cf5  What the system is \cf6 -\cf5  How components connect \cf6 -\cf5  How to work with the system \cf6 -\cf5  How to debug issues \cf6 -\cf5  How future AI sessions should collaborate with me --- \cf3 ## 1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW\cf5  \cf3 ### Components:\cf5  \cf6 -\cf5  
\f5\b **ChatGPT**
\f4\b0  \'97 generates valid HA automations in package YAML format. \cf6 -\cf5  
\f5\b **n8n Workflow**
\f4\b0  \'97 orchestrates the pipeline: \cf6 -\cf5  Collects user intent \cf6 -\cf5  Requests YAML from GPT \cf6 -\cf5  Sends JSON (file
\f6\i _name + automation_
\f4\i0 yaml) to HA \cf6 -\cf5  
\f5\b **Home Assistant Script (`write
\f7\i _automation_
\f4\i0\b0 and
\f6\i _reload`)**: - Calls shell_
\f4\i0 command to write the YAML file - Reloads automations - **Home Assistant Shell Command (`write_automation`)
\f5\b **: - Python one-liner writing files into `/config/packages/` - **
\f4\b0 Home Assistant Packages
\f5\b **: - All AI-generated automations live here - Loaded automatically at startup or reload ### Data Flow (end to end): User \uc0\u8594  ChatGPT \u8594  YAML \u8594  n8n \u8594  HA Script \u8594  File Write \u8594  automation.reload \u8594  Live Automation --- ## 2. FILE LOCATIONS ### Home Assistant
\f4\b0 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa85\partightenfactor0

\f8\fs24 \cf2 /config/configuration.yaml\uc0\u8232 /config/scripts.yaml\u8232 /config/packages/ \u8592  AI-generated automations live here\u8232 /config/packages/gpt_automations/ (optional subfolder)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

